385
00:15:39,000 --> 00:15:41,740
Wait, Ichinose?! Our Ichinose?!

386
00:15:39,750 --> 00:15:41,460
Come to think of it

387
00:15:41,740 --> 00:15:46,680
When I heard the name, 
I did wonder if it was Yokko's friend.

388
00:15:44,210 --> 00:15:46,680
Yoko (Yokko)
Sasano's girlfriend

389
00:15:47,680 --> 00:15:49,140
Sorry about that

390
00:15:49,490 --> 00:15:52,220
Wait, wait, wait! Wait a sec!

391
00:15:52,220 --> 00:15:54,970
So that was Chizuru-san at our boozer?

392
00:15:54,970 --> 00:15:57,430
And you were hiding it from us?!

393
00:15:57,430 --> 00:15:58,730
Sounds like it.

394
00:15:58,730 --> 00:16:02,690
Oh, yeah! She was there
on that beach trip, too!

395
00:16:03,190 --> 00:16:12,410
What is with your nerves
(acting ability)?!

396
00:16:03,230 --> 00:16:05,460
That's so scary! It's basically horror!

397
00:16:05,460 --> 00:16:07,920
How can real life be so movie-like?!

398
00:16:07,700 --> 00:16:12,410
You only realized
now, Kuri?

399
00:16:07,920 --> 00:16:11,920
I-It just happened to turn out that way.

400
00:16:09,950 --> 00:16:12,410
It was all Mizuhara...

401
00:16:12,410 --> 00:16:14,070
Hang on.

402
00:16:13,410 --> 00:16:16,910
I can't
overlook this

403
00:16:14,070 --> 00:16:16,910
Does that mean Yokko still doesn't know?

404
00:16:15,160 --> 00:16:16,910
A masked friend?

405
00:16:17,300 --> 00:16:20,800
Oh, nah, I think that's 
her true self, anyway.

406
00:16:20,800 --> 00:16:22,380
She's not tricking her friends.

407
00:16:22,380 --> 00:16:26,000
Huh... I guess it's okay, then.

408
00:16:27,380 --> 00:16:31,010
It's gonna be hard to keep 
all this from her, though.

409
00:16:30,510 --> 00:16:35,470
She's my girlfriend

410
00:16:31,010 --> 00:16:33,820
I-I'll ask about it.

411
00:16:33,260 --> 00:16:35,470
Ask Chizuru!

412
00:16:33,820 --> 00:16:35,470
ASAP, pls.

413
00:16:36,700 --> 00:16:40,770
<i>It's become such a big deal that it's 
gonna be hard ironing out the wrinkles.</i>

414
00:16:36,980 --> 00:16:40,770
It's quite the
predicament

415
00:16:37,980 --> 00:16:40,770
My bad, Kuri

416
00:16:38,980 --> 00:16:40,770
The ripples

417
00:16:41,140 --> 00:16:43,940
How should I face her if 
I run into her on campus?

418
00:16:42,000 --> 00:16:46,280
<i>We're third-years, huh? 
Things will start to change.</i>

419
00:16:43,940 --> 00:16:49,030
Eh, lots of people work in secret. 
Just be normal, man.

420
00:16:44,270 --> 00:16:52,120
Sasa-pai's
a fourth-year now

421
00:16:46,790 --> 00:16:49,760
<i>I gotta make sure I don't 
cause any more problems.</i>

422
00:16:49,030 --> 00:16:52,120
I dunno if I can without 
thinking about it.

423
00:16:54,020 --> 00:16:54,660
Yo.

424
00:16:54,660 --> 00:16:56,080
Heya, Kibe.

425
00:16:56,520 --> 00:16:58,170
Whatcha talking about?

426
00:16:58,170 --> 00:17:02,170
Just about how Chizuru-san's 
actually the Ichinose from Literature.

427
00:17:02,460 --> 00:17:04,380
Oh, yeah, right.

428
00:17:04,670 --> 00:17:06,870
Wait, you knew?!

429
00:17:06,870 --> 00:17:10,010
How could you not put it together 
after hearing her name?

430
00:17:08,380 --> 00:17:10,010
What are you,
an ace detective?

431
00:17:10,370 --> 00:17:12,050
Heya, Kazu-chin.

432
00:17:12,050 --> 00:17:13,540
H-Hey.

433
00:17:15,230 --> 00:17:16,510
<i>Kibe...</i>

434
00:17:16,860 --> 00:17:19,500
Apparently, avocados can 
heal erectile dysfunction.

435
00:17:17,200 --> 00:17:19,040
<i>It's been four months.</i>

436
00:17:19,040 --> 00:17:20,880
<i>We're interacting normally,</i>

437
00:17:19,500 --> 00:17:20,880
Where'd that come from?

438
00:17:20,880 --> 00:17:25,420
<i>but it feels like we're both 
trying to avoid the topic.</i>

439
00:17:23,980 --> 00:17:26,330
We're gonna swing by the club room.

440
00:17:25,420 --> 00:17:27,100
<i>It's kinda awkward.</i>

441
00:17:26,330 --> 00:17:27,340
See ya.

442
00:17:27,340 --> 00:17:28,690
Bye.

443
00:17:29,060 --> 00:17:30,810
<i>Now we're alone!</i>

444
00:17:31,950 --> 00:17:33,640
What do you have next, Kazu-chin?

445
00:17:33,640 --> 00:17:36,160
O-Organizational Management Theory.

446
00:17:36,160 --> 00:17:38,480
We can head to B Wing together, then.

447
00:17:38,480 --> 00:17:39,790
Y-Yeah.

448
00:17:40,430 --> 00:17:43,860
<i>But it makes sense, given what came out.</i>

449
00:17:43,860 --> 00:17:49,260
<i>Just apologizing in front of everyone 
won't make things go back to normal.</i>

450
00:17:50,020 --> 00:17:53,060
<i>He's one of the people 
I made look bad the most.</i>

451
00:17:53,060 --> 00:17:56,320
<i>He didn't show up for dinner 
after that at Hawaiians, either.</i>

452
00:17:56,770 --> 00:18:00,520
<i>He probably feels like 
I betrayed his trust.</i>

453
00:18:00,990 --> 00:18:07,110
Watching you does make me feel like 
I want to be friends with believers.

454
00:18:07,410 --> 00:18:10,150
So what's all this, you little punk?!

455
00:18:10,910 --> 00:18:14,250
<i>There's no going back for us anymore.</i>

456
00:18:14,860 --> 00:18:16,570
I'm sorry, Kibe!

457
00:18:17,030 --> 00:18:19,540
I'm sorry for lying about 
Chizuru for so long!

458
00:18:22,680 --> 00:18:26,910
I tried to tell you so many times, 
but I didn't have the strength.

459
00:18:26,910 --> 00:18:28,460
And look what it led to.

460
00:18:28,770 --> 00:18:32,550
I swear, I wasn't trying 
to trick you or anything!

461
00:18:38,920 --> 00:18:41,360
I'm not holding a grudge over 
something from four months ago.

462
00:18:41,360 --> 00:18:42,680
I have better things to do.

463
00:18:44,510 --> 00:18:49,110
Awkward guys get called that 'cause they 
can't handle too many things at once.

464
00:18:49,650 --> 00:18:53,700
Of course, some do hit the big time 
and gain money and influence,

465
00:18:53,700 --> 00:19:00,580
but most people try to protect 
what's dear to them as best they can.

466
00:19:01,070 --> 00:19:05,890
To be honest, it hurt when I thought 
you were lying to me the whole time.

467
00:19:05,890 --> 00:19:09,580
Sure, I was jealous of you walking 
around with a hottie like that,

468
00:19:09,580 --> 00:19:13,670
but mostly I was happy for you, 
and I thought you two were a good match.

469
00:19:14,230 --> 00:19:20,270
I also believed that our talks had gone 
past "frank" into "crude" territory.

470
00:19:20,270 --> 00:19:24,660
And I felt ridiculous for not even 
searching "Mizuhara Chizuru" online.

471
00:19:25,500 --> 00:19:28,780
But she's your girlfriend now, right?

472
00:19:28,780 --> 00:19:31,570
That must mean you share a special bond.

473
00:19:32,230 --> 00:19:37,780
When I figured she's more important to 
you than I am, everything fell into place.

474
00:19:38,670 --> 00:19:39,830
Kibe...

475
00:19:40,800 --> 00:19:45,830
Hey, everyone lies for 
the things they care about.

476
00:19:45,830 --> 00:19:48,210
It doesn't mean they do it out of malice.

477
00:19:48,690 --> 00:19:52,820
I was just wrong about how incapable 
I thought you were of lying.

478
00:19:52,820 --> 00:19:55,800
It doesn't mean I don't still 
consider you a good guy.

479
00:19:56,360 --> 00:20:01,140
Now, all I think is I'll take a chainsaw 
to your guts if you ever break up.

480
00:20:01,570 --> 00:20:05,600
Relax. I'll crush your skull, 
even if I become a zombie.

481
00:20:05,990 --> 00:20:08,330
Man, I don't wanna go to class.

482
00:20:08,330 --> 00:20:09,190
<i>I see...</i>

483
00:20:09,730 --> 00:20:12,940
<i>He feels that way, even though 
I did him dirty by lying?</i>

484
00:20:12,940 --> 00:20:14,260
<i>Kibe!</i>

485
00:20:14,260 --> 00:20:16,390
Y-You're not serious, are you?

486
00:20:16,390 --> 00:20:18,660
I'll press your balls into a bookmark.

487
00:20:18,930 --> 00:20:20,030
Bookmark?

488
00:20:20,030 --> 00:20:22,030
Formalin's not cheap, y'know.

489
00:20:25,530 --> 00:20:29,330
I think it can wait until after you've 
come to terms with your own feelings.

490
00:20:39,860 --> 00:20:43,180
You're such a bro, Kibe!

491
00:20:41,050 --> 00:20:43,640
BFFs forever

492
00:20:44,130 --> 00:20:49,100
<i>Seriously, anybody but him 
would've cut ties with me.</i>

493
00:20:49,870 --> 00:20:53,610
<i>But I'm still lying 
about us being a couple.</i>

494
00:20:53,610 --> 00:20:56,200
<i>I haven't made it up to him yet.</i>

495
00:20:56,200 --> 00:21:00,070
<i>If that gets out, he'll be well 
within his rights to skewer me alive.</i>

496
00:21:00,070 --> 00:21:01,530
<i>Yeah, not yet.</i>

497
00:21:01,900 --> 00:21:03,070
I'm going to look into it.

498
00:21:03,070 --> 00:21:04,660
I'll give it a real shot.

499
00:21:04,970 --> 00:21:05,960
<i>We're on the way!</i>

500
00:21:07,120 --> 00:21:11,080
Breaking

501
00:21:07,120 --> 00:21:11,080
Ruins Excavation in Barcelona

502
00:21:07,520 --> 00:21:10,570
<i>Regarding the excavation 
project in Barcelona,</i>

503
00:21:10,570 --> 00:21:12,950
<i>the survey team on the scene...</i>

504
00:21:14,790 --> 00:21:16,960
<i>Are we really on the way?!</i>

505
00:21:16,960 --> 00:21:19,660
<i>Mizuhara hasn't gotten 
in touch for a week now.</i>

506
00:21:18,550 --> 00:21:23,390
She did say she had no idea

507
00:21:19,660 --> 00:21:23,390
<i>What if she's stuck right after 
she started her investigation?!</i>

508
00:21:19,800 --> 00:21:23,390
how to go about it!!

509
00:21:23,390 --> 00:21:25,510
<i>Or maybe she has her answer already!</i>

510
00:21:25,510 --> 00:21:27,890
I looked into it more, 
and you get 1 point.

511
00:21:26,510 --> 00:21:27,890
It went down

512
00:21:28,140 --> 00:21:32,100
boing                       boing

513
00:21:28,340 --> 00:21:30,170
Gah, I'm so worried!

514
00:21:28,770 --> 00:21:32,100
Fish on the
cutting board

515
00:21:29,640 --> 00:21:32,100
So much so that I might
just send her a
LIVE message asking wyd?

516
00:21:30,170 --> 00:21:33,500
More worried and terrified 
than I've ever been!

517
00:21:33,500 --> 00:21:35,310
I wonder if Yaemori-san's in.

518
00:21:35,310 --> 00:21:36,970
I'll go talk to her...

519
00:21:38,940 --> 00:21:40,740
<i>Mizuhara!</i>

520
00:21:40,740 --> 00:21:42,010
You startled me.

521
00:21:41,450 --> 00:21:43,160
She was about to
ring my doorbell?!

522
00:21:42,010 --> 00:21:43,160
S-Sorry.

523
00:21:43,160 --> 00:21:44,680
Were you about to head out?

524
00:21:44,680 --> 00:21:48,180
Nah, just airing the place out. 
I wanted a taste of the fresh spring air.

525
00:21:44,910 --> 00:21:49,370
Our windows are pretty tiny

526
00:21:46,160 --> 00:21:49,370
This is the problem
with run-down apartments

527
00:21:48,180 --> 00:21:49,370
So you're free, then?

528
00:21:49,370 --> 00:21:50,840
Yeah, what's up?

529
00:21:50,840 --> 00:21:53,500
<i>Mizuhara?! What does she want?!</i>

530
00:21:53,800 --> 00:21:56,590
I wanted you to come over for a bit.

531
00:21:56,590 --> 00:21:57,800
Huh?

532
00:21:57,800 --> 00:21:59,330
<i>What?!</i>

533
00:21:59,330 --> 00:22:00,940
What cute wallpaper.

534
00:22:00,940 --> 00:22:02,370
Where's the bedroom?

535
00:22:01,050 --> 00:22:06,550
This is way beyond "investigation"!

536
00:22:02,370 --> 00:22:04,610
You're making me blush. I love you.

537
00:22:04,610 --> 00:22:06,550
<i>Come over?!</i>

538
00:22:06,850 --> 00:22:09,680
<i>Are you sure you want it to be so sudden?!</i>

539
00:22:09,310 --> 00:22:13,770
I'm not ready for this

540
00:22:09,680 --> 00:22:13,770
<i>I get that you need to check, 
but it's too soon for this!</i>

541
00:22:10,560 --> 00:22:13,770
I mean, I'll go...

542
00:22:14,400 --> 00:22:16,860
Wh-What's wrong? Do you have a leak?

543
00:22:14,770 --> 00:22:16,860
butt

544
00:22:17,130 --> 00:22:19,890
Wait, no. When I say 
"come over," I mean...

545
00:22:20,860 --> 00:22:22,030
to my grandma's place.

546
00:22:24,530 --> 00:22:25,430
Wha?

547
00:23:57,480 --> 00:24:01,570
I'm so glad my Kazuya 
got back on his feet!

548
00:24:01,570 --> 00:24:03,220
Sorry for making you worry.

549
00:24:03,220 --> 00:24:07,180
You should be! As punishment, 
heal my heart and soul!

550
00:24:07,180 --> 00:24:07,790
Hug!

551
00:24:07,790 --> 00:24:09,930
Hey, stop that! We're on the clock!

552
00:24:09,930 --> 00:24:11,030
Get away from me!

553
00:24:11,030 --> 00:24:15,260
Oh, no more, Kazuya! 
We'll get kicked off the air!

554
00:24:15,260 --> 00:24:17,720
I'm not doing anything, okay?!

555
00:24:17,720 --> 00:24:19,820
Anyway, next time on <i>Rent-a-Girlfriend</i>:

556
00:24:19,820 --> 00:24:20,880
"Childhood Home and...

557
00:24:20,880 --> 00:24:21,520
...Girlfriend."

558
00:24:21,520 --> 00:24:24,470
We're talking about a home 
and raising a child?

559
00:24:23,520 --> 00:24:27,030
"Childhood Home and Girlfriend"

560
00:24:24,470 --> 00:24:26,770
Hold your horses, Kazuya!

